# L §5.14 A hole in a term: "Only the parts the take could reach under some reading of the holes merge ...; a part
# ranked after enough certainly-ranked parts to cover the outflow stays known."  The order is lexicographic (§5.12):
# a first term that is known and differs ranks two arcs whatever a later hole term says.  sav's order is (if w in
# taxes and k.owner == ania_tomek then 0 else 1), rank[k.owner], rank a hole.  Ania's 1 000.00 and Tomek's 500.00
# (inheritances) and the couple's 50.00 (interest).  q1: the tax of 7.00 on 2025-07-01 ranks the couple's part first
# under every reading of rank and is covered by it: 43.00 left (scratch/exp_lex.py), the others known.  q2: the tax of
# 63.00 on 2025-08-01 takes the couple's 43.00 whole, and its other 20.00 falls between Ania's and Tomek's parts,
# which only rank orders: one hole part of 1 480.00 that may be either's, the couple's part known at 0.
# (Was one hole part of the whole balance at q1: the migrator's same_and_reach.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2025-12-31
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-12-31

source src "test"
unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
kind couples: parties
kind persons: parties
kind inheritances: transfers
  attr heir: key persons
kind interests: transfers
kind taxes: transfers
kind savings: place DUK min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(DUK)
  takes k for w order (if w in taxes and k.owner == ania_tomek then 0 else 1), rank[k.owner]
place sav: savings lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2000-01-01..
input wz: observed
def rank[p in parties]: int = ?"which money leaves the savings first?" at reader
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule community = (if p == ania_tomek then 1 else 0)
  rule inherited beats community = (if p == m.heir then 1 else 0) when m in inheritances

ask q1: bal(sav, 2025-07-01) of ania_tomek, bal(sav, 2025-07-01) of ania, bal(sav, 2025-07-01) of tomek
ask q2: bal(sav, 2025-08-01) of ania_tomek, bal(sav, 2025-08-01) of ania, bal(sav, 2025-08-01), bal(sav, 2025-08-01) of tomek

version cast
  cite src
  known 2025-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1991-03-14..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1989-07-02..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2016-09-10..

version stmt
  cite src
  governs 2025-01..2025-12
  known 2025-01-01
  covers sav
  opening[sav] = 0 at 2025-01-01 start
  wz[w1] = (on: 2025-06-16, kind: inheritances, leg cash from world to sav amount 1000.00 DUK, heir: ania) "l1"
  wz[w2] = (on: 2025-06-16, kind: inheritances, leg cash from world to sav amount 500.00 DUK, heir: tomek) "l2"
  wz[w3] = (on: 2025-06-30, kind: interests, leg cash from world to sav amount 50.00 DUK) "l3"
  wz[w4] = (on: 2025-07-01, kind: taxes, leg cash from sav to world amount 7.00 DUK) "l4"
  wz[w5] = (on: 2025-08-01, kind: taxes, leg cash from sav to world amount 63.00 DUK) "l5"
=== expect
q1: (43.00 DUK, 1 000.00 DUK, 500.00 DUK)
...
q2: (0.00 DUK, ?"sav: 1 480.00 DUK may be ania's: which money leaves the savings first?" (sav), 1 480.00 DUK, ?"sav: 1 480.00 DUK may be tomek's: which money leaves the savings first?" (sav))
...
